@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 500
hide footbox
title Ideator | problem solving and decisions\nDesigned workflow — current saved setup; runtime behavior not verified
actor User as U
participant "Ideator" as I
participant "Fresh web\nevidence" as W
database "Run report(s)\nand board" as R
participant "One-time\ncheck-ins" as T

U -> I : Problem statement + optional run knobs
note over U,I
Required: problem. Defaults: 5 ideas / challenge, 4 tests, 5 sources; markdown; auto.
Country: explicit > problem / research > US; language: explicit > message > English.
Only mode persists. Save every phase, score and decision to the report(s).
end note

== Diamond 1: explore the problem, then focus ==
group Discover — divergent
I -> W : Research problem, customer voice and competitors\nFind and cite sources-knob distinct sources; market-focused
W --> I : Findings + source links
I -> I : Derive evidence-grounded challenges and sticky notes\nUnsourced claims are labeled hypotheses
end
group Define — convergent
I -> I : Rate possible and exciting (each 1–5)\nRank by sum; propose at most 5 challenges
alt ask mode
I -> U : Ranked challenges: choose or steer
U --> I : Selected challenges / direction
else auto mode
I -> I : Select top 5; ties: exciting, then possible\nRecord picks and reasons
end
end

== Diamond 2: explore solutions, then focus ==
group Develop — divergent
I -> I : Generate ideas-knob ideas per selected challenge\nFit market culture, habits and rules
end
group Deliver — convergent
I -> I : Score and rank all ideas; pick at most 5\nMix ideas into concepts
note over I,R
Weighted = (cheap + simple) × evidence × uniqueness, 1 decimal.
Cheap / simple: 1–5. Evidence: 1.3 / 1.15 / 1.0, with source IDs.
Uniqueness: 1.2 / 1.1 / 1.0. Ties: evidence > uniqueness > simple > cheap;
then ID order, explicitly labeled unresolved / arbitrary.
end note
alt ask mode
I -> U : Ranked ideas + concepts: choose concepts to pretotype
U --> I : Approved concepts
else auto mode
I -> I : Choose top 2 concepts by mean constituent idea score\nTies: mean evidence level, then number of ideas
end
end

== Test design and delivery — not proof of demand ==
I -> I : Design pretotypes-knob tests across selected concepts\nBest concept first; at least one each when count allows
I -> R : Save hypotheses, success numbers, deadlines, go/no-go rules\nRecommend first test per concept + ready-to-use materials
note over U,I
People run tests. Ideator drafts, never sends / posts / publishes materials.
Materials: market language + report language if different.
end note
alt ask mode
I -> U : Which tests will you run, and when do they start?
U --> I : Test selection and start dates / answer
else auto mode
I -> R : Mark recommended first tests selected\nState: check-in will be set up when start date is supplied
end
opt start date is known
I -> T : Schedule one-time check-in: day after each test deadline
end
I -> R : Complete report(s), key results and PNG board\nOne shared title across board, MD heading, HTML h1 / title
I -> U : Single final delivery: problem + 7 knobs + result line\nPNG board + requested MD, HTML, or both

== Later: human-run tests and evidence-based follow-up ==
opt start date supplied after delivery
U -> I : Selected tests + start date
I -> T : Schedule check-in for day after each deadline
end
U -> U : Run selected pretotypes with real users
T -> I : Deadline + 1 day: check-in fires
I -> U : Ask for test results
U --> I : Observed results
I -> I : Compare results with success number\nRecommend go, no-go, or iterate
I -> R : Record outcome in every report; refresh key results / board
I -> T : Delete completed check-in

legend bottom
Ask mode waits at all three gates; auto mode runs through materials, board and delivery.
Cancellation at any point: stop, mark reports CANCELLED, delete run check-ins.
endlegend
@enduml
